0..79 Comment "// A record type\'s faces: each a set of the record\'s labels, named in a `where`"
80..158 Comment "// block after the type. A static bracket after the type fixes some fields, by"
159..179 Comment "// label or by face."
180..182 Comment "//"
183..260 Comment "// A record type\'s labels are its boundary, and a face over them names a part"
261..337 Comment "// of the record. The checker checks each fixed value at its field\'s type. A"
338..414 Comment "// value of the patched type is the record of its free fields, and a literal"
415..495 Comment "// can state a fixed field at its fixed value. A value of the record type stands"
496..573 Comment "// at the patched type when each fixed field converts with its fixed value. A"
574..639 Comment "// name at it reads a fixed field as the value the bracket fixes."
640..642 Comment "//"
643..720 Comment "// The block names each face as a theory\'s `face` member does. The block ends"
721..800 Comment "// the type member at its `}`, as a `data` block ends its declaration. A record"
801..869 Comment "// type with no block keeps its labels as its boundary all the same."
870..938 Comment "// `Config[.port = 443, .tls = true]` fixes two fields by label, and"
939..1015 Comment "// `Config[secure ↦ *{.port = 443, .tls = true}]` fixes the face `secure`."
1016..1047 Comment "// `|->` spells `↦` in ASCII."
1048..1050 Comment "//"
1051..1129 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr` — a face past the labels, a"
1130..1209 Comment "//   face named twice, a bracket naming a field or a face the type lacks, and a"
1210..1270 Comment "//   literal stating a fixed field at another value, refused"
1271..1350 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/shaped-signature.gandr` — a theory\'s `boundary` and its"
1351..1361 Comment "//   faces"
1362..1431 Comment "// - owes: #5579 — an element of a patched type coerced back to the"
1432..1450 Comment "//   configuration"
1451..1531 Comment "// - owes: #5106 — two faces fixed at once, whose values agree where the faces"
1532..1541 Comment "//   meet"
